  "query_preview": "..\n\nThrough Sunday..\n\nIn general, upper ridging over the region will bring mostly dry \nand warm conditions for the next several days.\n\nA cold front dropping through the area early this morning will\nbring cooler conditions and less wind to the area today than\nSunday. Highs in the 50s to lower 60s can be expected, with an \nisolated shower or two over northwestern areas into the morning \nhours. Winds increase a bit tonight along the western foothills as\npressure gradients tighten ahead of an approaching shortwave. \nWind gusts from Livingston to Nye in the 20 to 40 mph range can \nbe expected. The aforementioned shortwave will push through the \narea on Tuesday bringing breezy westerly winds and showers (15-30%\nchance, greatest over the mountains). Widespread wind gusts of 20\nto 40 mph can be expected, with areas along the western foothills\npotentially seeing wind gusts to 50 mph. Currently, the \nprobability for exceeding 50 mph is 25% at Livingston, 30% at Big \nTimber, and 60% for Harlowton. Will continue to monitor, though \nwinds look to remain below the need for a wind highlite at this \ntime.\n\nWednesday through Saturday, upper ridging builds over the region\nbringing warmer and drier conditions. Highs will increase to the\nupper 50s to the 60s most days. Heading into Sunday, ensembles and\ncluster analysis show lower heights building into the region as \nupper troughing gradually pushes inland over the western US,\nbringing a breakdown of the upper ridge. STP",
